  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promotion of Good Agricultural Practises in common beans cultivation in Northern Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Based on the results of a feasibility study into the bean value chain and groundnut value chain in northern Zambia (2021), this project will provide the necessary knowledge and capacity training in Good Agricultural Practices (GAP) to local agro-entrepreneurs to increase their production of beans in northern Zambia. This knowledge and capacity training will lead to increased production of beans and a better organized local farmers cooperative. This will contribute to local food security, the growth of local private sector activity and trade. Regionally, this development will contribute to the further development of the Lake Tanganyika regional trade corridor.</narrative>
  </description>
